    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We sequenced 96 colorectal tumours and I have the somatic mutation matrix (tumours as rows, genes as columns), an exon-length table for the genes, a tab-delimited cancer gene list and a MSigDB pathway GMT. I'd like to sort the tumours into a handful of subtypes according to which pathways carry their mutations, trying between two and four subtypes. The aim is to see whether the subtypes line up with survival later on."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like to sort the tumours into a handful of subtypes according to which pathways carry their mutations, trying between two and four subtypes.\" -- the request does not say whether one item may belong to several groups at once: if one group each: SAMBAR; if several groups at once: no registered workflow gives this.\n2. \"The aim is to see whether the subtypes line up with survival later on.\" -- available from SAMBAR's output plus a step you run outside NetZoo: A test outside NetZoo with a clinical table keyed by sample ID.\n\nBefore I choose a workflow, please tell me: Should each gene, regulator or sample belong to one group only (one group each), or may one belong to several groups at once?\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
